    }
  ],
  "turns": [
    {
      "_id": "0",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 1,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Solve 5 times the quantity x minus 3, equals 2x plus 9, for x.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t001",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:00:00.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:08.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "1",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 2,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So there's an x on both sides, and a bracket to expand first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t002",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:08.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:37.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "2",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 3,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "We could expand the bracket first, or maybe try dividing through by something — thoughts?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t003",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:01:57.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "3",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 4,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Maybe we could guess a value and test it, but expanding seems safer.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t004",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:02:03.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:11.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "4",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 5,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's go with expanding the bracket then, that looks like the cleanest way in.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t005",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:16.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:46.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "5",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 6,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, let me start working it out.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t006",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:03:47.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:05.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "6",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 7,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead, expand the left side first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t007",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:04:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:06.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "7",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 8,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "5 times x is 5x, and 5 times negative 3 is negative 15, so 5x minus 15 equals 2x plus 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t008",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:05:07.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "8",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 9,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good, now let's move the x terms to one side.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t009",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:06:18.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:24.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "9",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 10,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Subtract 2x from both sides: 3x minus 15 equals 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t010",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:07:28.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "10",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 11,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Now add 15 to both sides.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t011",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:17.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:43.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "11",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 12,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "That gives 3x equals 24.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t012",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:08:43.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:45.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "12",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 13,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Nice, the equation is fully isolated for x now.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t013",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:09:53.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:34.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "13",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 14,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Wait, before dividing — why do we move the x terms and not the numbers first?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t014",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:10:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:35.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "14",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 15,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Good question — we group like terms so one side only has x, keeping the equation balanced.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t015",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:11:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:04.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "15",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 16,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So whatever we do to one side, we do to the other, that's why subtracting 2x kept it equal.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t016",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:07.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:45.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "16",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 17,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, and that same idea lets us divide both sides by 3 at the end.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t017",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:12:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:22.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "17",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 18,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So dividing 24 by 3 finishes it because balance was kept the whole way through.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t018",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:13:29.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:27.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "18",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 19,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's look back at the original equation once more before we wrap up.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t019",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:32.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:54.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "19",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 20,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "It says solve 5 times x minus 3 equals 2x plus 9.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t020",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:14:56.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:16.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "20",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 21,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, that's the equation we've been working with all along.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t021",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:19.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:31.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "21",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 22,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "What if we'd moved the 2x over first — would we land somewhere different?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t022",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:15:35.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:19.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "22",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 23,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Let's try that — subtract 2x from both sides before expanding fully.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t023",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:48.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "23",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 24,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Then we'd still get 3x minus 15 equals 9, so maybe the order doesn't matter.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t024",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:16:50.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:17:33.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "24",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 25,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Interesting thought — let's turn that into an actual plan.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t025",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:17:41.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:18:15.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "25",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 26,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the plan is to move the 2x first this time and see if we still get x equals 8.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t026",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:18:17.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:27.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "26",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 27,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Sounds good — what's the first move?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t027",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:33.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:19:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "27",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 28,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Subtract 2x from both sides of 5x minus 15 equals 2x plus 9 first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t028",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:20:03.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:21:11.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "28",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 29,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Then what comes after that?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t029",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:21:17.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:14.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "29",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 30,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Then add 15 to both sides and divide by 3, same as before.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t030",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:22:14.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:23:04.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "30",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 31,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go ahead and write both versions side by side on your sheet.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t031",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:23:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:23:49.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "31",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 32,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Okay, I've got them lined up in two columns.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t032",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:23:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:24:55.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "32",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 33,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Can you see them clearly on your screen?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t033",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:25:03.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:25:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "33",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 34,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Yes, it's all visible now.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t034",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:25:44.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:24.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "34",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 35,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Great, let's check the answer holds up.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t035",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:30.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:45.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "35",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 36,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me plug x equals 8 back into the original equation to check.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t036",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:26:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:19.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "36",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 37,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go for it, work out both sides.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t037",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:23.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:45.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "37",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 38,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "5 times 8 minus 3 is 5 times 5, which is 25.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t038",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:27:52.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "38",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 39,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "And the right side?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t039",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:22.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:41.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "39",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 40,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "2 times 8 plus 9 is 16 plus 9, which is 25 too, so it checks out.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t040",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:28:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:29:21.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "40",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 41,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "New problem: a recipe uses flour and sugar in a 3 to 5 ratio, and we're using 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t041",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:29:25.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:30:23.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "41",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 42,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So we need to find how much sugar goes with 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t042",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:30:24.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:31:08.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "42",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 43,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Right, that's exactly what we need to find.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t043",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:31:12.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:32:04.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "43",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 44,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So the ratio means for every 3 cups of flour there's 5 cups of sugar, right?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t044",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:32:07.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:13.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "44",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 45,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Exactly, the two amounts scale together by the same factor.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t045",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:16.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:48.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "45",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 46,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "So whatever the flour parts get multiplied by, the sugar parts scale the same way.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t046",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:33:49.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:01.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "46",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 47,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That's the key relationship we'll use to solve it.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t047",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:07.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:50.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "47",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 48,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Let me find what one part is worth first.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t048",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:34:53.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:06.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "48",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 49,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Go on, use the flour side.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t049",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:36.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "49",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 50,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "3 parts equal 12 cups, so one part is 12 divided by 3, which is 4 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t050",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:42.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:35:57.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "50",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 51,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "Now use that to find the sugar.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t051",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:36:01.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:07.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "51",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 52,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "Sugar is 5 parts, so 5 times 4 is 20 cups.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t052",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:11.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:49.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "52",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 53,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "So how much sugar is needed in total?",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t053",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:37:54.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:38:40.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "53",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 54,
      "role": "STUDENT_1",
      "content": "20 cups of sugar for 12 cups of flour.",
      "turn_id": "demo-a-s04-t054",
      "start_time": "2026-02-03T16:38:40.000Z",
      "end_time": "2026-02-03T16:39:35.000Z"
    },
    {
      "_id": "54",
      "session_id": "demo-a-s04",
      "sequence_id": 55,
      "role": "TUTOR",
      "content": "That gives us the amount we needed.",
